<title>CHINA: China aims to repeat 1996 record grain harvest.</title>
<headline>China aims to repeat 1996 record grain harvest.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>China aims to repeat its record grain harvest last year of 480 million tonnes in 1997, top agricultural officials at a conference in Beijing said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>China hoped to keep the area of land cultivated with cereal crops at no less than 110.7 million hectares in 1997, said officials at the close of a four-day Central Rural Work Conference organised by the Communist Party that ended on Monday.</p>
<p>Grain acreage in 1996 was 112.2 million hectares, an increase of 2.13 million hectares from 1995.</p>
